# understudy — consumer-identifier denylist (EXAMPLE)
#
# The `no-consumer-identifiers` lint scans `core/` for internal/consumer names that
# must never ship in the published, OSS harness. The denylist is CONSUMER-SUPPLIED so
# `core/` itself never embeds — and thus never publishes — those very names.
#
# Enable the guard for your project by providing your internal tokens via ONE of:
#   * env   UNDERSTUDY_FORBIDDEN_IDENTIFIERS="acme-internal,widgetco pipeline"
#   * env   UNDERSTUDY_FORBIDDEN_FILE=/path/to/denylist.txt
#   * copy this file to  .understudy-forbidden.local  (gitignored, auto-loaded from CWD)
#
# Format: one literal token per line. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are
# ignored. Runs of separators (- _ . / whitespace) match flexibly, so `acme-pipeline`
# also catches `acme pipeline`, `acme/pipeline`, `acme_pipeline`. Case-insensitive.

acme-internal
widgetco pipeline
INTERNAL_API_KEY_PREFIX
